st of the carpet and padding needed to cover it.\n\n1. **Identify the shape of the room:**\n   The diagram shows a room that can be divided into two rectangles. The first rectangle has dimensions 4 yds by 5 yds (left side), and the second rectangle has dimensions 5 yds by 2 yds (right side).\n\n2. **Calculate the area of each rectangle:**\n   - For the first rectangle:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area}_1 = 4 \\, \\text{yds} \\times 5 \\, \\text{yds} = 20 \\, \\text{square yds}\n     \\]\n   - For the second rectangle:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area}_2 = 5 \\, \\text{yds} \\times 2 \\, \\text{yds} = 10 \\, \\text{square yds}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the total area of the room:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total Area} = \\text{Area}_1 + \\text{Area}_2 = 20 \\, \\text{square yds} + 10 \\, \\text{square yds} = 30 \\, \\text{square yds}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the cost of the carpet for the total area:**\n   The cost of the carpet is \\$21.95 per square yard.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of Carpet} = 30 \\, \\text{square yds} \\times 21.95 \\, \\$/\\text{square yd} = 658.50 \\, \\$\n   \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the cost of the padding for the total area:**\n   The cost of the padding is \\$2.55 per square yard.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Cost of Padding} = 30 \\, \\text{square yds} \\times 2.55 \\, \\$/\\text{square yd} = 76.50 \\, \\$\n   \\]\n\n6. **Calculate the total cost (carpet + padding):**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total Cost} = 658.50 \\, \\$ + 76.50 \\, \\$ = 735.00 \\, \\$\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total cost of the carpet and padding needed to exactly cover the room is \\(\\boxed{735.00}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{735.00}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
